<title>SOUTH AFRICA: IBCA reaffirms Standard Bank ratings.</title>
<headline>IBCA reaffirms Standard Bank ratings.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>International rating agency IBCA said on Wednesday it had reaffirmed both the international and domestic ratings for Standard Bank of South Africa (SBSA) and its holding company Standard Bank Investment Corp Ltd (Stanbic).</p>
<p>SBSA has a domestic long-term rating of AA and a short-term rating of A1+. Both SBSA and Stanbic have individual international ratings of B, the highest assigned to a South African bank along with that of Investec Bank Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
